---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CohortStrip from '../components/CohortStrip.astro';
import core from '../data/core.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const c = core.counts;
---
<Base current="home">
  <div class="wrap-wide" style="padding-top: 3rem;">
    <div class="wrap" style="padding-left: 0; margin-left: 0;">
      <p class="eyebrow">A digital history of India–Korea Buddhist exchange</p>
      <h1>Buddhist Bridges</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Sixteen centuries of Buddhist exchange between India and Korea —
        {c.people_carried} documented mediators, five generations, one five-hundred-year silence.
      </p>
    </div>

    <CohortStrip />

    <div class="wrap" style="padding-left: 0; margin-left: 0;">
      <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">There was never one bridge</h2>
      <p>
        The Buddhist connection between India and Korea is usually told as a single continuous
        stream — an unbroken transmission from the land of the Buddha to the peninsula. The
        documented record says otherwise. It was built <strong>five times, by five different kinds
        of mediator, in alternating directions</strong>: Silla monks walking west to India before
        900; an Indian master and his Korean disciples in Goryeo; colonial intellectuals whose
        bridges were made of paper, not journeys; a thin postwar thread; and, since the 1990s,
        an institutional web of orders, universities, relic returns, and pilgrimages in both
        directions. Between the second bridge and the third lies Joseon&rsquo;s five-hundred-year
        documented silence — not missing data, but a finding.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Why it matters:</strong> the record periodizes a relationship usually told as myth
        or modern diplomacy, and shows a religious connection surviving five centuries of closed
        borders through texts and lineage rather than travel — until institutions, in our own
        era, rebuilt the bridge of bodies.
      </p>

      <div class="doors">
        <a class="door" href={`${base}/argument/`}>
          <p class="door-title">Follow the argument</p>
          <p>The five bridges in five chapters — with the people, journeys, texts, and
          institutions that carried each one, and the evidence behind every claim.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="door" href={`${base}/timeline/`}>
          <p class="door-title">Explore the evidence</p>
          <p>The full interactive timeline, the prosopographical register of all
          {c.people_carried} mediators, period network views, and the complete source registry.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="provenance">
        {c.people_carried} mediators · {c.events} events · {c.institutions} institutions ·
        {c.texts} texts · {c.sources} graded sources · every claim cited to a record ID and a
        resolvable source · dataset frozen and checksummed (V3.0, 2026-08-17) ·
        <a href={`${base}/data/`}>data &amp; method</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
